	)
	(text "This AON-powered hardware chain grants two latched permissions.\nGLOBAL_PWR_PERMIT enables the switched MIRA supplies; MATRIX_PERMIT\nallows the downstream matrix and programming circuits to operate.\nA fault clears permission and requires an explicit re-arm."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 45.44 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.45 1.45)
				(thickness 0.15)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "05abc3c1-d22c-4944-9e4b-1b99f0b53b18")
	)
	(text "Explicit rising-edge re-arm after a fault"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 57 192.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.85 0.85)
				(thickness 0.15)
				(color 0 70 190 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "080077fc-f1dd-41ff-885d-62c0502f06a0")
	)
	(text "Global fault chain\nClears all switched-rail permission"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 18 70.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.85 0.85)
				(thickness 0.15)
				(color 0 70 190 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1ec42f11-a820-4b44-b775-4566b6449d5b")
	)
	(text "Matrix fault chain\nRequires rails, commands and host ready"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 18 129.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.85 0.85)
				(thickness 0.15)
				(color 0 70 190 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2288d5e6-35b1-4b5c-8bef-7193af2102b8")
	)
	(text "U2601 combines the global conditions; U2602 combines matrix conditions.\nTheir outputs drive the two active-low clears of U2603. With D HIGH\nand preset inactive, a rising PWR_ARM_PULSE or MATRIX_ARM_PULSE\nsets the corresponding permission only while its clear is HIGH."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 91.16 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.45 1.45)
				(thickness 0.15)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "263f6001-d127-4369-8a15-a9711c167c6e")
	)
	(text "Inputs and outputs"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 63.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 100 110 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "28ed1525-8bb8-4973-ac6e-2a3738e0b118")
	)
	(text "R2602/R2605 (10 kOhm) pull the stop lines HIGH; closing J2601/J2602\nor asserting a kill GPIO pulls them LOW. R2601/R2604/R2606/R2607\n(100 kOhm) hold kill and arm inputs LOW when released. There is no\nRC delay: firmware must send clean arm edges after conditions settle."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 114.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.45 1.45)
				(thickness 0.15)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "35c06398-98f0-46a9-a073-00df18c24cec")
	)
	(text "A global fault clears both permissions; a matrix fault clears only\nmatrix permission. Fault recovery alone does not re-arm either latch.\nAON_RESET_N must clear U2603 during startup. The stop connectors\ntrip when closed; an open cable is not detected as a stop."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 136.88 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.45 1.45)
				(thickness 0.15)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4154b980-ba7f-49de-8364-b9ae87961cfb")
	)
	(text "Timing and settings"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 109.22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 100 110 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "653a7d79-78c2-4e39-99e0-facdec3c30d5")
	)
	(text "Hardware permit interlocks"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 26.24 0)
		(effects
